In the latest episode of The A.V. Club &#8216;s Undercover series that arrived Thursday (Jan. 15), the members of the interplanetary rock group &#8212; dressed in their signature fantastical, slightly terrifying alien costumes &#8212; put their own spin on the glitzy dance-pop anthem, swapping in edgy guitars, pummeling drums and screamo-style vocals. Just for the occasion, guitarist Mike Derks/Balsac the Jaws of Death strapped a pink hobby horse to his costume

&#8220;God, what have you done?/ You&#8217;re a pink pony girl/ And you dance at the club,&#8221; belts frontman Mike Bishop (aka Blöthar), likely tearing up his vocal cords in the process. &#8220;Oh mama, I&#8217;m just having fun/ On the stage in my heels/ It&#8217;s where I belong.&#8221;

The cover comes a couple of months ahead of GWAR&#8217;s 2026 tour kickoff in March. With dates running through the end of April, the group&#8217;s Gor-Gor Strikes Back Tour will find them traveling to various American cities to &#8220;destroy your town,&#8221; per GWAR&#8217;s website , where ticket info is also available. The band&#8217;s seven-track The Return of Gor Gor project dropped in July.

Roan, on the other hand, has stayed more lowkey in 2026 so far after a busy 2025, much of which she spent on tour. She also picked up two new Billboard Hot 100 hits last year, first with &#8220;The Giver,&#8221; which peaked at No. 5 in March, and then with &#8220;The Subway,&#8221; which debuted at No. 3 in August.

